=== entry 8f3b71a7aa44
kind: translation
rules: invoke
intent: Following ketchup names the ketchup skill, with no slash, and keeps the sibling link. The window's cutoff is the message before the user typed the invocation, so both invocations give their Codex form. Everything else stays verbatim.
--- upstream
Follow [`/ketchup`](../ketchup/SKILL.md), but show what happened in a short silent video instead of its summary and visuals. Its window starts at the last message the user wrote before `/ketchup-video`, not before any earlier `/ketchup`. Writing and rendering the video, outside the repo, is the one exception to its read-only rule. The reply is ketchup's opening sentence, the embedded video, one line naming any work left that you can do yourself, and the action items. When the video shows a call's options, call each option by the name the video gives it. If the render fails, say so in one line and give only the calls.
--- patched
Follow the [**ketchup**](../ketchup/SKILL.md) skill, but show what happened in a short silent video instead of its summary and visuals. Its window starts at the last message the user wrote before `/ketchup-video` (`$ketchup-video` in Codex), not before any earlier `/ketchup` (`$ketchup` in Codex). Writing and rendering the video, outside the repo, is the one exception to its read-only rule. The reply is ketchup's opening sentence, the embedded video, one line naming any work left that you can do yourself, and the action items. When the video shows a call's options, call each option by the name the video gives it. If the render fails, say so in one line and give only the calls.
